# Copy to .env (or run `npm run setup`, which writes .env for you and verifies
# the key). Everything here is optional in the sense that the tool degrades
# honestly without it — each skipped capability says so in its output rather
# than pretending.

# ScrapingBee. Used only as an escalation path when a site rejects direct,
# honestly-identified fetches (e.g. a 403 on the homepage). Without it, direct
# fetches still work and blocked sites are reported as blocked.
SCRAPINGBEE_API_KEY=

# Anthropic. Turns on rephrase-only narration of the findings prose in live
# reports (lib/narrate.js). Without it, deterministic prose ships — complete
# and identical in substance. The model never assigns scores either way.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Lead capture webhook (e.g. a Google Apps Script bound to a Sheet whose
# doPost appends the posted JSON as a row). Leads always also land in
# out/leads.jsonl, with or without this.
#LEADS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Cloudflare Turnstile. BOTH are needed to enforce the email gate; set neither
# and the gate stays soft and reports 'not-enforced' on every lead row, which is
# the shipped default.
#
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is PUBLIC. It is rendered into the teaser page markup, which
# is what a site key is for, and it only works on the hostnames configured at
# Cloudflare. Setting it also adds one third-party script to that page, and the
# page's own footer says so when it does.
#
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is NOT public and must never enter a tracked file. On
# Render it is set in the dashboard; locally it goes in .env, which is gitignored.
#
# Cloudflare publishes dummy keys for testing (they work on any hostname):
#   sitekey 1x00000000000000000000AA  / secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA  always passes
#   sitekey 2x00000000000000000000AB  / secret 2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA  always fails
# A test secret accepts ONLY the dummy token and rejects real ones, and vice versa.
#
# If the site key is set but the secret is not, the widget renders and the server
# still does not enforce it — the honest half-configured state, reported as
# 'not-enforced' rather than as a pass.
#TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
#TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Server port for `npm run serve` (default 8787).
#PORT=8787

# Incumbent-vendor index, used ONLY by the private lead score (lib/incumbent.js
# -> lib/lead-score.js). It is never rendered to a visitor. data/ is gitignored
# and does not ship with a clone, so a fresh checkout has no index: the loader
# then returns { missing: true } and the lead score simply carries no incumbent
# signal. Nothing in the public grade, findings or reports depends on it.
#
# Leave this UNSET to use the default, <repo>/data/incumbent-index.json. Set it
# only to point at a copy kept somewhere else.
#
# Suffixes peel right to left: .json, .json.gz and .json.gz.b64 all load the
# same object. That is not a convenience. The plain index is ~5.2MB; Render caps
# the COMBINED size of a service's secret files at 1MB, and its secret-file UI
# is a paste-in Contents field for plaintext, so raw gzip bytes do not survive
# it. gzip-then-base64 is the only form that fits AND pastes:
#     node tools/build-incumbent-secret.js      -> ~200KB, ready to paste
# Then INCUMBENT_INDEX=/etc/secrets/incumbent-index.slim.json.gz.b64
#
# When this is unset AND no default file exists, the lookup reports
# incumbent_status 'no_index_loaded' -- meaning NO SEARCH RAN. That is
# deliberately a different answer from 'no_evidence_in_index', which means a
# search ran and found nothing. Never collapse the two.
#INCUMBENT_INDEX=/absolute/path/to/incumbent-index.json
